1
00:00:13,596 --> 00:00:16,516
North latitude, 28 degrees 24 minutes,

2
00:00:16,599 --> 00:00:20,103
west longitude, 80 degrees 36 minutes.

3
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,940
Wait for the next new moon.

4
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:28,153
Heaven will appear then.

5
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:31,114
I have no use for this place now.

6
00:00:31,614 --> 00:00:35,577
The birthed creature now belongs to me.

7
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:38,038
Jailhouse Lock.

8
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:41,291
You can only remember
three new pieces of information.

9
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:43,668
What do I need to do?

10
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:45,211
What's important to me?

11
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:47,255
What shouldn't I forget?

12
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:51,426
I have things I need to tell Jolyne!

13
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:58,475
What am I doing here?

14
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:02,187
Something's off.

15
00:01:07,942 --> 00:01:12,864
What? Why is this man
going inside the house?

16
00:01:12,947 --> 00:01:14,949
I have no idea what's going on.

17
00:01:15,033 --> 00:01:16,576
Bitch!

18
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:18,787
Stop rewinding it so much!

19
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:21,456
No shit, now I'm lost too!

20
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:23,458
Get this bitch out of here!

21
00:01:24,501 --> 00:01:27,045
Fine, I'll leave.

22
00:01:29,714 --> 00:01:33,468
Greenie, that's the head honcho of
all the other spiders in this cell.

23
00:01:33,551 --> 00:01:37,931
Hello sir, great to meet you.

24
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:40,391
I'm Pit Viper Ron.

25
00:01:40,475 --> 00:01:43,102
Yes, good to meet you.

26
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:46,606
And this spider right here's
about to croak.

27
00:01:46,689 --> 00:01:49,067
Oh, hey.

28
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:51,027
The hell?

29
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:54,030
What's funny about it?

30
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:56,950
I don't get this comic at all.

31
00:01:57,033 --> 00:02:01,496
Oh, why did I come to
this recreation room?

32
00:02:03,206 --> 00:02:05,375
2. YOU CAN ONLY RETAIN
UP TO THREE NEW PIECES OF INFORMATION

33
00:02:05,458 --> 00:02:07,627
That's right… I'm in a predicament.

34
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:11,881
I came here to find a way
out of this situation.

35
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,263
The medical wing is beyond this corridor.

36
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:20,723
The stairs on the way
lead to Emporio's room.

37
00:02:20,807 --> 00:02:22,851
It's usually not a hassle,

38
00:02:22,934 --> 00:02:25,019
but the area is heavily guarded today.

39
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:27,647
How can I reach Emporio?

40
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:41,286
IF ANYONE KEEPS LOOKING AT
MY LEFT HAND, DON'T HESITATE

41
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:44,122
JUST PUNCH

42
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:50,753
She has a Stand!

43
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:52,672
It looks familiar too.

44
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:55,675
I have to chase it. She's my enemy!

45
00:02:55,758 --> 00:02:57,677
She's the Stand User!

46
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:35,775
EPISODE 24: JAILBREAK…

47
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:10,310
Where… am I?

48
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:13,396
And who was I trying to chase just now?

49
00:05:13,479 --> 00:05:14,397
There she is.

50
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:17,650
- Target found at the corner of D-12-2.
- Hands in the air!

51
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:21,612
I was wrong, I'm the one being chased!

52
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:26,492
She's right there! Hey, don't move!

53
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,375
What the…

54
00:05:34,459 --> 00:05:37,462
Was there just one guard
coming from this way?

55
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:39,964
No, that doesn't matter right now.

56
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,966
Where is this?

57
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,510
Where the hell am I?

58
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:46,137
Why am I being chased?

59
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:08,576
Where is she? I swear she ran this way!

60
00:06:08,659 --> 00:06:10,328
Keep looking. We have to find her!

61
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:11,704
There's no way we lost her.

62
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:13,539
She must be hiding somewhere close!

63
00:06:13,623 --> 00:06:15,416
She may have ran towards the stairs.

64
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,667
That's not possible.

65
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:19,087
She would have to walk right past us.

66
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:20,171
Stairs?

67
00:06:20,671 --> 00:06:22,215
"Go see Emporio…"

68
00:06:22,715 --> 00:06:27,053
That's right, that flight of stairs
leads to Emporio's room.

69
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:46,155
What's going on?

70
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:49,700
That's right, I spilled some water.

71
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:51,953
GO TELL JOLYNE

72
00:06:52,620 --> 00:06:56,374
I have to tell Jolyne.

73
00:06:57,667 --> 00:06:59,293
I have to print something.

74
00:06:59,377 --> 00:07:01,254
We'll end up forgetting it,

75
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:04,215
so I have to show her the guard's face.

76
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:07,760
Or else, I can't tell her.

77
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:09,011
MEW MEW, AGE 25
LEAD GUARD

78
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:13,182
Jolyne Cujoh.

79
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:17,103
You can't retain more than
three new pieces of information.

80
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:19,480
Even if you saw four guards,

81
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:22,567
you can't remember more
than three of them.

82
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:26,112
Even though the fourth guard
is in your line of sight,

83
00:07:26,195 --> 00:07:29,365
your brain rejects it
since that's too much to remember.

84
00:07:31,409 --> 00:07:35,580
You wanted to go see Emporio,
so I let you guide me here.

85
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:36,789
So I see.

86
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:39,167
I didn't know there was a room here.

87
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:52,597
Emporio!

88
00:07:56,976 --> 00:07:59,187
Jolyne.

89
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:01,689
- How long have you been here?
- I got here just now.

90
00:08:01,772 --> 00:08:05,151
Your poor hands. What happened to them?

91
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:07,320
The writings on your arms…

92
00:08:07,403 --> 00:08:09,363
You can only remember three new things.

93
00:08:09,447 --> 00:08:11,991
You're in the same boat as I am!

94
00:08:12,074 --> 00:08:13,868
Ever since that time
in the confinement cell!

95
00:08:13,951 --> 00:08:17,121
That's right, I was hoping to see you.

96
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:21,167
I have to tell you something, Jolyne!

97
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:23,294
What's this? What was I doing just now?

98
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:27,298
What? Jolyne?

99
00:08:27,381 --> 00:08:28,799
When did you get here?

100
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:32,595
- And why did you come?
- Right, why am I here?

101
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:34,305
- Why?
- Why?

102
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:37,517
Oh, that's right. I'm here to see you.

103
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:39,268
I don't know what for,

104
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:42,480
but there was a really serious reason
for me to come see you.

105
00:08:42,563 --> 00:08:43,940
Print it out.

106
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:45,942
I have to print something out.

107
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:48,528
If I don't, it'll be forgotten forever.

108
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:50,404
Printing is the only way to remember it.

109
00:08:50,488 --> 00:08:52,406
Print what out, Emporio?

110
00:08:52,490 --> 00:08:54,450
What are you talking about?

111
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:57,870
Huh? But how would I do that?

112
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:01,123
What was I trying to print out?

113
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:05,795
"Mew Mew, Lead Guard."

114
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:08,005
It makes sense now.

115
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:12,468
So he was with you
when my Stand activated.

116
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:16,472
He had seen my face and heard me
say my name.

117
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:20,017
Emporio was hiding in the walls of
the confinement cell.

118
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:22,520
Usually, I'd let him be.

119
00:09:23,020 --> 00:09:28,401
My Jailhouse Lock's job
is to keep Stand Users behind bars.

120
00:09:28,484 --> 00:09:30,403
But if he's trying to leave
a record of me,

121
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:32,029
then that changes everything.

122
00:09:32,113 --> 00:09:34,282
I now deem you an escapee.

123
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:45,793
Her Stand, Stone Ocean.
Bullets won't give her a scratch.

124
00:09:45,876 --> 00:09:52,300
But her memory would have been impaired
had I fired four shots.

125
00:09:52,383 --> 00:09:55,052
Her brain wouldn't even register
the fourth shot,

126
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:59,265
let alone the smoke from it!

127
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:02,727
Jolyne…

128
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:05,187
What?

129
00:10:05,271 --> 00:10:08,065
I don't know why there's a room
in a place like this,

130
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:11,193
and what a little boy is doing here.

131
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:13,696
But Pale Snake had told me

132
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:18,117
that Jolyne Cujoh has allies
from the inside who have been helping her

133
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:20,328
- using walkie-talkies and the like.
- Emporio!

134
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:22,622
So this little boy was her ally.

135
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:26,792
And now, any record he had
about me is gone.

136
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:29,462
I won't forgive you!

137
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:31,839
Wow, how caring.

138
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:34,050
But even that anger you feel right now

139
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:37,928
will be completely forgotten
with the next three pieces of information.

140
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:40,848
That's my Stand Jailhouse Lock's ability.

141
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:43,934
Take this. Meet your end, Jolyne Cujoh!

142
00:10:48,356 --> 00:10:51,233
You won't be able to see
more than three of the shots.

143
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:54,195
The others will leave a hole in your body!

144
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:10,920
An image reflected on water
is the one whole truth.

145
00:11:11,003 --> 00:11:13,339
You might be able to shoot
many shots at once,

146
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:16,008
but I can see their reflections
all at once.

147
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:19,470
I hope you haven't forgotten
about this one.

148
00:11:19,553 --> 00:11:20,846
AVENGE EMPORIO

149
00:11:26,394 --> 00:11:27,311
That bitch…

150
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:30,147
But I managed to destroy the computer.

151
00:11:30,231 --> 00:11:32,066
Now, I just have to escape.

152
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:36,028
Jolyne will forget about me soon anyway.

153
00:11:36,112 --> 00:11:38,322
She will never be able to
remember who I am!

154
00:11:42,618 --> 00:11:44,912
Emporio, hang in there
for just a bit longer.

155
00:11:44,995 --> 00:11:46,580
I will go after her.

156
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:51,043
Don't, Jolyne.

157
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:54,839
You'll forget everything the moment
you step out of this room.

158
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:58,467
You'll even forget about defeating her.

159
00:11:58,551 --> 00:11:59,510
So, please…

160
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:04,306
Emporio, I understand
why you are so careful.

161
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:08,269
It was a skill you needed to develop
to survive inside these prison walls.

162
00:12:09,061 --> 00:12:12,189
But there comes a time
when we have to move forward,

163
00:12:12,773 --> 00:12:14,775
even if that means facing danger.

164
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:17,820
And for me,

165
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:20,156
that time is now!

166
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:24,201
Is this her string?

167
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:35,921
STAND NAME: JAILHOUSE LOCK
STAND USER: MEW MEW

168
00:12:42,428 --> 00:12:44,722
Why am I injured?

169
00:12:45,973 --> 00:12:49,101
But there comes a time
when we have to move forward,

170
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:51,979
even if that means facing danger.

171
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:54,648
I don't know why…

172
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:57,985
but I feel like there's something
I have to do…

173
00:12:58,694 --> 00:12:59,695
What was it?

174
00:13:01,071 --> 00:13:03,574
That's right, print it out.

175
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:05,576
I have to tell Jolyne.

176
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:07,870
I have to print something out…

177
00:13:09,038 --> 00:13:12,541
but what was I trying to print?

178
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:16,420
My room doesn't even have a printer.

179
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,380
COMPUTE

180
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:27,473
She's strong!

181
00:13:30,142 --> 00:13:31,644
She is the enemy I'm after.

182
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:34,605
I can't let her get away.

183
00:13:38,567 --> 00:13:40,653
I need you back here!

184
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:42,363
I'm at the D10 stairwell!

185
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:48,577
Look, she's over there!

186
00:13:48,661 --> 00:13:50,496
Lead Guard Mew Mew is being assaulted!

187
00:13:50,579 --> 00:13:51,413
The gate!

188
00:13:51,497 --> 00:13:52,623
Open the gate!

189
00:14:05,886 --> 00:14:06,804
This place…

190
00:14:06,887 --> 00:14:09,306
Why am I here?

191
00:14:11,141 --> 00:14:14,228
Hurry! Capture her!

192
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:15,938
Am I…

193
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:17,398
being chased?

194
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:22,361
The three guards are here now.

195
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:27,032
Now, you will never recall that I exist!

196
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:37,126
Now, try to run away just a little bit.

197
00:14:37,209 --> 00:14:39,587
Then, the guards will shoot you to death.

198
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:42,339
Before you go, those hands of yours…

199
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:44,925
I almost forgot that
they can block gunshots.

200
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:57,354
My duty is strictly to keep
Stand Users confined in this facility.

201
00:14:58,397 --> 00:15:00,983
But I feel great right now.

202
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:07,281
It feels great to
watch you get shot to death.

203
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:09,199
Because you brought this upon yourself.

204
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:13,245
You wanted to walk out of your line,
so this is what you get.

205
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:14,163
There she is.

206
00:15:14,246 --> 00:15:20,377
And I love that you can't see
more than three guards!

207
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:23,505
- I've found her!
- There she is!

208
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:27,676
No one can escape my Jailhouse Lock!

209
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:33,140
Jolyne…

210
00:15:33,223 --> 00:15:34,516
How long have you been here?

211
00:15:35,017 --> 00:15:37,269
Emporio, it's you!

212
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:38,646
I have to tell you…

213
00:15:38,729 --> 00:15:41,982
I have to print this out for you.

214
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:44,360
If I don't, you won't be able to
remember her.

215
00:15:44,443 --> 00:15:45,736
Print it out?

216
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:47,821
Binaries.

217
00:15:47,905 --> 00:15:50,032
These are binaries made up
of ones and zeroes.

218
00:15:50,115 --> 00:15:51,867
I must have computed this.

219
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:55,371
You can print it correctly.

220
00:15:55,454 --> 00:15:58,999
We are going to imprint it
into your memory!

221
00:15:59,833 --> 00:16:02,586
Stone Ocean!

222
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:10,636
They're binary numbers.

223
00:16:10,719 --> 00:16:13,305
The binary system can express anything.

224
00:16:13,889 --> 00:16:17,017
Draw zeroes and ones using your thread.

225
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:18,811
You can use Stone Ocean

226
00:16:18,894 --> 00:16:21,522
as a printer that can express images!

227
00:16:28,278 --> 00:16:30,990
Can I consider you my enemy?

228
00:16:31,073 --> 00:16:33,117
Are you an enemy?

229
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,243
What?

230
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:37,287
She's talking nonsense.

231
00:16:37,871 --> 00:16:39,248
She can't even see me.

232
00:16:39,748 --> 00:16:42,084
Now, be gone.

233
00:16:42,876 --> 00:16:47,756
Thanks. So I guess
you are an enemy after all.

234
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:57,808
What's happening?

235
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:01,520
She has Mew Mew hostage!

236
00:17:01,603 --> 00:17:02,896
Emporio.

237
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:06,608
Her Jailhouse Lock is no longer active.

238
00:17:07,276 --> 00:17:09,862
Yes. I'm okay now.

239
00:17:09,945 --> 00:17:12,906
Great. I'm leaving now.

240
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:15,868
Like I told you before,
I'm leaving this prison.

241
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:18,287
What are you going to do?

242
00:17:18,370 --> 00:17:22,416
If you plan on staying here,
then you should go back to your room.

243
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:31,341
Jolyne, my time to leave is now.

244
00:17:31,842 --> 00:17:33,218
I…

245
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:35,095
I want to see the outside world!

246
00:17:37,389 --> 00:17:39,516
Look, a child.

247
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:41,685
Why is there a child in prison?

248
00:17:41,769 --> 00:17:43,771
Either way, keep your guard up!

249
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:56,408
Come, Emporio. Let's go.

250
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:59,578
Excuse me.

251
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:02,790
Sorry, coming through.

252
00:18:06,293 --> 00:18:08,629
Sorry, excuse me.

253
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:14,551
What? Who was I trying to gun down?

254
00:18:14,635 --> 00:18:18,430
- What am I doing here?
- Why am I here?

255
00:18:19,598 --> 00:18:21,391
Great job, Mew Mew.

256
00:18:21,475 --> 00:18:23,268
I'm glad you understand.

257
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:28,440
First, we are going to the medical wing
to treat Emporio's wound.

258
00:18:29,316 --> 00:18:32,236
I'm counting on you to keep us safe,
Jailhouse Lock.

259
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:35,572
An undefeated ability
that restricts the enemy's memory.

260
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:40,410
Where… am I?

261
00:18:46,583 --> 00:18:48,335
Do you have my father's disc?

262
00:18:48,418 --> 00:18:50,879
Yes. I've had it with me the entire time.

263
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,631
Hey, Jolyne!

264
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:55,050
It's Jolyne.

265
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:56,301
Emporio, you too.

266
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:57,511
Ermes.

267
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:04,810
I heard a commotion.
I knew it had to be you guys.

268
00:19:05,811 --> 00:19:06,854
Who is she?

269
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,981
She is this prison's lead guard.

270
00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:10,315
What?

271
00:19:10,816 --> 00:19:12,609
Does that mean you're…

272
00:19:12,693 --> 00:19:16,613
Yes. We are breaking out.
We're about to leave this place.

273
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:19,658
You're going after that priest.

274
00:19:19,741 --> 00:19:21,160
That's right, Ermes.

275
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:26,623
I have to seal what he took.
I'm ready for anything.

276
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:30,294
Things even worse than
what we faced in this prison.

277
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:38,969
Take me with you then.

278
00:20:30,938 --> 00:20:34,816
Father, thank you.

279
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,194
I don't mean to be rude,
but are you feeling okay?

280
00:20:37,277 --> 00:20:40,155
Yes, I'm just a little tired.

281
00:20:47,287 --> 00:20:48,580
Are you… sure?

282
00:20:52,125 --> 00:20:53,502
Excuse me.

283
00:21:02,678 --> 00:21:04,763
What is this?

284
00:21:08,058 --> 00:21:10,560
What's wrong with these eggs?

285
00:21:12,312 --> 00:21:13,647
A Stand…

286
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:18,860
Pale Snake is no longer my Stand ability.

287
00:21:19,486 --> 00:21:22,614
Something else is inside me… but what?

288
00:21:23,198 --> 00:21:25,158
I feel terrible…

289
00:21:25,242 --> 00:21:28,620
Something is running loose inside me.

290
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:32,582
This power, it's beyond my control.

291
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:35,836
But this power carries hope.

292
00:21:35,919 --> 00:21:39,339
I can at least feel
hope within this power.

293
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:42,968
Dio's memo inside Jotaro's memory…

294
00:21:43,552 --> 00:21:46,930
It seems this power needs
the things in that memory.

295
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:48,682
Time and place.

296
00:21:49,933 --> 00:21:52,269
North latitude, 28 degrees 24 minutes.

297
00:21:52,352 --> 00:21:54,855
West longitude, 80 degrees 36 minutes.

298
00:21:55,355 --> 00:21:58,275
That's where heaven will be.

299
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:02,654
This location is Cape Canaveral.

300
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:04,698
Kennedy Space Center.

301
00:22:09,036 --> 00:22:10,704
It will be during the new moon.

302
00:22:11,204 --> 00:22:12,664
Six more days.

303
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:46,299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
